{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487184-w20-armor-dexterity-penalty","id":1487184,"title":"W20 Armor Dexterity Penalty","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-20T06:59:12-07:00","id":1487184,"title":"W20 Armor Dexterity Penalty","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Quick question, the Dex penalty for armor types, it is a difficulty increase, or a dice pool reduction?<br /> <br /> On M20 and V20 it is a dice pool reduction but W20 p. 291 makes me think that on W20 is a difficulty increase.<br /> <br /> Any help is welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-20-2022, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T10:23:11-07:00","id":1487205,"title":"","content":"It's a copy paste from Werewolf Revised (206). There is also increases difficulties rather than lowering dicepools. This is most likely because Armor wearing opposition is quite more likely in Werewolf than in most other game lines, and considering that mooks have small dicepools, high penalties would eviscerate them even nastier than a rampaging Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T18:06:57-07:00","id":1487292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487184-w20-armor-dexterity-penalty?p=1487205#post1487205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a copy paste from Werewolf Revised (206). There is also increases difficulties rather than lowering dicepools. This is most likely because Armor wearing opposition is quite more likely in Werewolf than in most other game lines, and considering that mooks have small dicepools, high penalties would eviscerate them even nastier than a rampaging Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answer. I have been checking the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1OK1pf7N3tIoPYYhX0kL37s-awQ0owwKNZlopwZ4EjHI/edit#gid=0\" target=\"_blank\">probability dice table</a>, and increasing the difficulty lowers your chances more than lowering your dice.<br /> <br /> For example, lets say you have 5 dice between Dex and Firearms, no specialty, and you want to compare both scenarios. Looking at the table for 5 dice at difficulty 6, gives: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Success chance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">84.4%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Failure chance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">13.49%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Botch chance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2.1%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Average successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2.4</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> If I lower the number of dice by 3 but keep the same difficulty it becomes: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Success chance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">65%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Failure chance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">26%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Botch chance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Average successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1.4</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> If I increase the difficulty by 3 but keep the number of dice: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Success chance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">49.4%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Failure chance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">34.64%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Botch chance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">15.96%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Average successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1.5</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> You actually make the mooks better by removing dice, not by increasing diff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-21-2022, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T04:45:50-07:00","id":1487360,"title":"","content":"You may be correct, but it's what the books say. It's also what 2nd edition Werewolf says. Now the question is if there was a mechanical implication behind it or it just seemed like a good idea at the time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"",